Given, ${g_{at\,high}} = {g_{at\,depth}}$

We know, ${g_{depth}} = g$\left( {1 - $\frac{d}{R}$} \right) 

$\therefore g$\left( {1 - \frac{d}{R}} \right)$ = {{GM_e} \over {{{(R + h)}^2}}} \Rightarrow g$\left( {1 - \frac{d}{R}} \right)$ = {{G{$M_e$}} $\over$ {{{$\left( {R + \frac{R}{2}} \right)$}^2}}}$ =  \frac{4}{9}${{G{$M_e$}} $\over$ {{$R^2$}}}$ =  \frac{4}{9}$g $\Rightarrow   \frac{d}{R}$ = 1 - $\frac{4}{9}$ = $\frac{5}{9}

$$\begin{aligned} & M_E=9 M_P \\\\ & R_E=2 R_P \end{aligned}$$ 

Escape velocity $=\sqrt{\frac{2GM}{R}}$

For earth $v_e=\sqrt{\frac{2 G M_E}{R_E}} $\begin{aligned} & \text { For } P, v_e=\sqrt{\frac{\frac{2 G M_E}{9}}{\frac{R_E}{2}}}=\sqrt{\frac{2 G M_E}{R_E} \times \frac{2}{9}} \\\\ & =\frac{v_e \sqrt{2}}{3} \end{aligned}
